   <owl:Class rdf:ID="pdbx_domainCategory">
      <rdfs:subClassOf>
         <owl:Class>
            <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
               <owl:Class rdf:about="#Category"/>
               <owl:Restriction>
                  <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="#has_pdbx_domain"/>
                  <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minCardinality>
               </owl:Restriction>
            </owl:intersectionOf>
         </owl:Class>
      </rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:equivalentClass rdf:resource="PDBo:pdbx_domainCategory"/>
   </owl:Class>
   <owl:Class rdf:ID="pdbx_domain">
      <rdfs:label>pdbx_domain</rdfs:label>
      <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">
Data items in the PDBX_DOMAIN category record information
about domain definitions.

A domain need not correspond to a completely polypeptide chain;
it can be composed of one or more segments in a single chain,
or by segments from more than one chain.

    Example 1 -
&lt;VRPTx:pdbx_domainCategory&gt;
   &lt;VRPTx:pdbx_domain id="d1"&gt;
      &lt;VRPTx:details&gt;Chains A, B&lt;/VRPTx:details&gt;
